Square table, read by antidiagonals, where row e.g.f.s, R(n,x), satisfy: d/dx log( R(n,x) )/n = R(n+1,x) with R(n,0) = 1; that is, the logarithmic derivative of the e.g.f. of row n, divided by n, equals the e.g.f. of row n+1, for n>=1.

